## closureKinds 1351 {"standing": "Which closure kind each closure-bearing field admits. Stated so no field is left to guess.", "byField": {"subject-scope.enumeratorClosure": "provider", "view.producerClosure": "provider", "fact.producerClosure": "provider", "finding.ruleClosure": "detector", "evaluation-seal.evaluatorClosure": "evaluator", "proof-bundle.evaluatorClosure": "evaluator", "import.producerClosure": "provider", "import.adapterClosure": "adapter", "stage-spec.producerClosure": "provider", "cache-key.producerClosure": "provider", "TypeScriptToolClosureV1.closureId": "toolchain", "ToolClosureV1.closureId": "toolchain", "toolchain.typescriptStdlibMerkleRoot": "stdlib", "toolchain.rustcDevLlvmDigest": "rust-dev-llvm", "SyntaxGrammarBundleV1.closureId": "grammar"}, "note": "No new closure kind is invented for producer acts: enumeration, view production, fact production and stage production are all provider acts under the existing kind. `grammar` is a genuinely new INSTALLED-COMPONENT kind, in the same family as `toolchain`, `stdlib` and `rust-dev-llvm`: the syntax-only mode's body interpreter is a bundled grammar set, and binding it to an existing kind would either claim it is a toolchain (it executes no compiler) or leave the component that interprets a body span outside the closure law, which is the one thing every other universe pins down."}
## normalizationSpecificationLaw 2234 {"standing": "Normative; consumed by identity Run closure's clones body-identity join (consumer24 S2). It replaces 'normalisationVersion names any retained blob' with one owner and one location per level.", "record": {"bundle": "identity", "selector": "#/$defs/normalization-specification-map"}, "closureTreePath": "opensip-interface/normalization/specification-map.v1.json", "owner": "The closure that INTERPRETS the body span, named by the fact sourceUniverse's admitted native context through the universe row's languageVersionBinding.normalizationClosure: TypeScript and Rust toolClosure.closureId (kind toolchain), syntax grammarBundle.closureId (kind grammar). Exactly one closure owns the map for a body; no other closure's map, and no retained blob outside a map, is consulted.", "joins": ["the owning closure's tree has a member at closureTreePath (BODY_NORMALIZATION_MAP_MISSING); promised bytes that are absent are retention loss, not a refusal of the claim", "those bytes are C(record) of a valid normalization-specification-map whose levels are strictly ascending (BODY_NORMALIZATION_MAP_INVALID)", "the payload normalisationLevel has a row (BODY_NORMALIZATION_LEVEL_UNMAPPED)", "that row's specificationDigest equals the payload normalisationVersion, so a specification of another level cannot stand in (BODY_NORMALIZATION_LEVEL_VERSION_MISMATCH)", "that digest is itself a member of the same closure's tree, so a map cannot point outside its own closure (BODY_NORMALIZATION_SPECIFICATI
## bodyEligibilityLaw 2447 {"standing": "Normative; consumed by the native Coverage producer boundary and identity Run closure (through scopeCapabilityLaw) and by the execution-inputs expected-source census (foundation/execution-inputs-contract.v1.md section 5).", "definition": "A snapshot path is BODY-ELIGIBLE under a native semantic universe exactly when its own suffix matches that universe row's languageVersionBinding.bodyEligibility. Form `dialect-table`: a key of the same row's closed dialect table (longest match still selects the variant; it does not change eligibility). Form `closed-suffix-set`: a member of `suffixes`. Eligibility is a property of the path and the universe DOMAIN only.", "independentOf": "Ownership, program membership, selected compilation targets, grammar selection, resolution and extraction outcome never make an eligible path ineligible. A .rs file no selected Cargo target compiles, a .ts file outside programRootFiles and a .ts file whose grammar the syntax universe did not select all stay eligible. Whether the universe could read such a path is decided by its owning prerequisite (compilation ownership, grammar capability) and disclosed on Coverage; it is never decided by dropping the path from what is owed.", "census": "For a relation carrying bodyIdentityJoin in the relation registry (today `clones`), the expected source-path subjects of a native coverage account are the ELIGIBLE paths of that cell's file inventory under the universe domain of the cell's languageMode. Config
## scopeCapabilityLaw 5300 {"standing": "Normative, and consumed by BOTH the native producer admission boundary and identity Run closure. It states what a COVERAGE claim over a body-dialect relation means under a universe whose dialect form is a closed suffix table. The per-BODY selector (`dialect.onUnknown`) was already total, but it is only reached while a body is being derived, so a scope that produced NO fact was classified by nothing and could claim a determinate `complete` for a path the universe cannot read in any dialect. Coverage is a claim about the EXAMINATION and must not be decided by whether the examination happened to produce output.", "appliesToDialectForm": "closed-suffix-table", "appliesToBodyEligibility": "Every native semantic universe. The suffix question is asked of the universe row's languageVersionBinding.bodyEligibility (bodyEligibilityLaw), not of its dialect form: for a closed-suffix-table dialect (TypeScript, syntax) the eligible suffixes ARE that table, and for the selected-compilation-target-edition dialect (Rust) they are the row's closed suffix set. appliesToDialectForm keeps its historical value for the first case; a Rust clones scope over Cargo.toml is now disclosed exactly as a TypeScript clones scope over package.json is, and a .rs path that no selected target compiles is still eligible and keeps the ownership law's own treatment.", "gate": "Relations carrying a `bodyIdentityJoin` in the relation registry, which is where the dialect axis is consulted at all. Nothing 
## languageVersionBindingLaw 1355 "Normative, and consumed by identity Run closure. The languageVersion component of a FACT-IDENTITY body frame is the RAW 32 BYTES of SHA-256(C(body-language-version)) - the same fixed-width treatment the inherited grammar already gives levelVersion, so the inherited frame bytes and field grammar are unchanged and the component is bounded for every valid input. Fixed width is not a convenience: the inherited frame gives each component a u8 length, and a component that embedded per-crate or per-package data is not representable for ordinary valid inputs. The record is DERIVED: closure rebuilds it from the universe ResolvedInputs, the admitted retained native context the universe own nativeContextId names, the enclosing fact own anchor and the retained nested records the universe commits, and compares. It carries the identity of the component that INTERPRETS the body span plus the SELECTED source dialect, and nothing else: not operational platform, not paths, not names, not resolution inputs, not build tooling, not option synthesis, and no per-crate or per-package collection. Every language declares its dialect axis explicitly; there is no null branch and no unexamined default. A universe domain used by a clones fact with no binding refuses, and every dialect branch that cannot SELECT refuses with a distinct cause rather than guessing."
## closureMembership 1962 {"standing": "Plan selection bindings for authoritative inputs; companion to closureKinds. Unreferenced CAS blobs are not evaluation inputs.", "direct": {"subject-scope.enumeratorClosure": "Selected for each scope of an evaluated view.", "view.producerClosure": "Selected for each evaluated view.", "stage-spec.producerClosure": "Selected for each stage of the execution plan.", "cache-key.producerClosure": "Selected for a cache/regeneration key bound to the Plan.", "finding.ruleClosure": "Selected for each evaluated finding.", "evaluation-seal.evaluatorClosure": "Selected for the evaluation seal."}, "equalToDirect": {"fact.producerClosure": "The enclosing evaluated view.producerClosure.", "proof-bundle.evaluatorClosure": "The evaluation-seal.evaluatorClosure."}, "selectedThroughOtherInput": {"import.producerClosure": "plan.importIds, which retains the import record naming them; an import named by proof.evaluationInputRefs must itself be a plan.importIds member (UNSELECTED_EVALUATION_IMPORT).", "import.adapterClosure": "plan.importIds, which retains the import record naming them; an import named by proof.evaluationInputRefs must itself be a plan.importIds member (UNSELECTED_EVALUATION_IMPORT).", "TypeScriptToolClosureV1.closureId": "plan.nativeContextDigests and the registered context closureJoins.", "ToolClosureV1.closureId": "plan.nativeContextDigests and the registered context closureJoins.", "toolchain.typescriptStdlibMerkleRoot": "plan.nativeContextDigests and the registere
## scope 416 {"governs": "bare-64-hex-digest-fields", "schemaSelectors": {"pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}(?![\\s\\S])", "$ref": "#/$defs/Hash"}, "nullableAlternatives": "Apply to the non-null branch; the annotation may be on that branch.", "typedPrefixIdentities": "Outside this annotation scope. Resolve the typed prefix through the identity-and-evidence section 3 identity table; its hex suffix is not a separate bare digest field."}
